        "original_id": "d78cb0ad-e2dc-5d5d-aa62-5c2879d99137",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen, Michael Faraday\n- Organizations: University of Heidelberg\n- Products: Bunsen burner, laboratory burner\n- Topics: instrument making, electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist who lived from 22 September 1791 to 25 August 1867 and contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected an earlier laboratory burner design by Michael Faraday into the Bunsen burner.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- Robert Bunsen and his laboratory assistant, Peter Desaga, developed the Bunsen burner as an improvement on laboratory burners then in use.",
